{
  "borough": "Hackney",
  "application_type": "All Other",
  "decision": "Refused",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;p&gt;&lt;span id=&quot;docs-internal-guid-bbb4b1e7-7fff-bb24-7180-c7fd86bcec52&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;&quot;&gt;The proposed development, by reason of its excessive scale, bulk, and unsympathetic design would appear as a visually dominant and incongruous addition that fails to preserve or enhance the character and appearance of the site or the Brownswood Conservation Area. The proposed development would be contrary to Policies D3 (Optimising Site Capacity through the Design Led Approach) and HC1 (Heritage Conservation and Growth) of the London Plan 2021; Policies LP1 (Design Quality and Local Character) and LP3 (Designated Heritage Assets) of the Hackney Local Plan 2033 and the Brownswood Conservation Area Appraisal.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p style=&quot;list-style-type: decimal; font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre;&quot;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;list-style-type: decimal; font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre;&quot;&gt;&lt;ol&gt;&lt;/ol&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 1.38; text-align: justify; margin-top: 6pt; margin-bottom: 6pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:#ffffff;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;&quot;&gt;The proposed development, by reason of its inappropriate scale, height, and proximity to neighbouring properties, would result in adverse loss of light, increased sense of enclosure and an overbearing and obtrusive impact to the living conditions of adjoining residential properties. Accordingly, the proposal would cause unacceptable harm to the amenity of neighbouring occupiers, contrary to Policy LP2 (Development and Amenity) of the Hackney Local Plan 2033 and Policies D3 (Optimising Site Capacity through the Design Led Approach) of the London Plan 2021.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;"
  ],
